/// A transcript content section. Each kind carries an encapsulating background
/// that fills the full inner width of the transcript box (excluding the box's
/// own borders), so larger text blocks read as clearly separated, boxed regions
/// while short lines stay legible. Large blocks — the echoed prompt and model
/// reasoning — get their own distinct, subtle tint to pull them apart. Tool
/// calls and their results share one neutral, suitably black background so a
/// `→ tool: …` line and its `✓ … finished` result stay grouped, distinguished
/// by their green/red text colour rather than a differing background.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
enum Section {
    /// The user's prompt as echoed into the transcript (`You: …`). Distinct tint.
    Prompt,
    /// Model reasoning / thinking, already rendered dim. Distinct tint.
    Reasoning,
    /// A proposed tool call (`→ tool: …`). Shares the tool result background.
    ToolCall,
    /// A tool's finished result (success). Shares a suitably black background.
    ToolResult,
    /// A failed tool result (told apart from success by its red text colour).
    ToolResultFailure,
}

/// The encapsulating background for one [`Section`], tuned for a dark terminal.
///
/// Large blocks — the echoed prompt and model reasoning — each get their own
/// distinct, subtle tint so they read apart; tool calls and their results share
/// one neutral, suitably black background so an action and its result stay
/// grouped and are told apart by text colour alone. Every tint is intentionally
/// dark so it complements (rather than competes with) the foreground colour
/// coding, and the fill rides the per-line style that the bordered transcript
/// paints across the full inner width. Callers combine it with the section's
/// existing foreground via [`Style::patch`], keeping the foreground colour and
/// modifiers while filling in only the background.
fn section_background(section: Section) -> Style {
    Style::default().bg(section.background())
}

